loyee reflects an ownership culture.","financial_summary":["DiDi Global Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $14.8B market cap on $27.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are expanding by +12.4pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -31% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $750M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 15.48\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, thin -49.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 10% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI d